{"step_index":2348,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T16:50:40Z","input_tokens":174636,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":627,"content":"### Best CLI / Harness for Meta Models (Llama 3.1 / 3.2 / 3.3)\n\nFor serving and interfacing with Meta models, there are two premier options depending on whether you are running **local hardware** or **cloud/serverless**:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Gold Standards for Local / Self-Hosted Servers\n\n#### Option A: **`vLLM`** (Industry Standard for Linux Production Serving)\n* **What it is**: High-throughput, PagedAttention-powered inference engine with a built-in OpenAI-compatible API server.\n* **Why it's the best**: Fastest serving engine for Meta models on Nvidia GPUs; supports speculative decoding, tensor parallelism, and streaming chunk responses.\n* **CLI / Setup**:\n  ```bash\n  pip install vllm\n  python3 -m vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server \\\n      --model meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct \\\n      --port 8000\n  ```\n* **Integration**: Your `tched-router` can point straight to `http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1` using native OpenAI-compatible wire formats.\n\n#### Option B: **`Ollama`** (Best for Rapid Local CLI / Zero-Config Testing)\n* **What it is**: Self-contained Go + llama.cpp runtime with clean model pulling and an instant local API server.\n* **CLI / Setup**:\n  ```bash\n  ollama run llama3.3\n  # Automatically serves an OpenAI-compatible endpoint on localhost:11434\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 2. What About Paseo?\n\n* **Paseo** is primarily the **Polkadot / Kusama testnet network** for Web3 / Substrate parachain consensus (which fits decentralized Web3 identity and smart contract anchoring).\n* If you meant **serving Meta models on a dedicated Web3/decentralized compute network**, platforms like **Akash Network**, **Render**, or **Bacalhau** allow you to spin up vLLM containers on decentralized GPUs.\n* If you are referring to a specific LLM harness tool named Paseo, **vLLM** and **SGLang** remain the authoritative high-performance production serving engines for Meta models on Linux.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Recommended Architecture for 3tched\n\nThe cleanest setup for your conglomerate:\n1. **Host a local vLLM (or Ollama) server** on an available GPU box or cloud VPS.\n2. In `tched-router` (`crates/tched-router` or `/etc/runit/tched-router`), configure the provider route to target that endpoint.\n3. Your containers call through **Door `:8090`**, which routes queries through `tched-router` directly into the Meta model server."}
