{"step_index":2350,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T16:51:10Z","input_tokens":2364,"cache_read_tokens":172514,"output_tokens":460,"content":"**OpenCode** (often used alongside OpenCode Interpreter / OpenCode CLI) is a fantastic, open-source terminal-first AI coding agent harness.\n\nHere is how it fits and why it works well for Meta models:\n\n---\n\n### What OpenCode Gives You\n\n1. **Terminal-Native CLI Harness**:\n   * Like Claude Code or Aider, but 100% open-source and model-agnostic.\n   * Runs directly in your terminal, inspects local files, executes shell commands, and handles multi-turn coding sessions.\n2. **First-Class Local Model Support**:\n   * Works out of the box with Meta models (Llama 3.1 / 3.3, CodeLlama) via **Ollama**, **vLLM**, or **OpenAI-compatible local endpoints**.\n   * You don't have to send your codebase to OpenAI or Anthropic—everything can stay local to your machine.\n3. **Can You Run It as a Server?**:\n   * OpenCode itself is primarily an interactive **client/agent harness** (CLI).\n   * **The Setup**: You run **vLLM** or **Ollama** as the background inference *server*, and point OpenCode at it as the *interactive coding harness*:\n     ```bash\n     # 1. Start your local Meta model server (e.g. Ollama or vLLM)\n     ollama serve\n     \n     # 2. Point OpenCode to your local server\n     export OPENAI_API_BASE=\"http://localhost:11434/v1\"\n     export OPENAI_API_KEY=***"local\"\n     opencode --model llama3.3\n     ```\n\n---\n\n### Why It Fits Our Conglomerate Model\n\n* Because OpenCode respects local environment configurations and POSIX filesystems, you could run it **inside a 3tched container**:\n  * It can read and write files directly through the **FUSE spine (`/run/opdbus/lungs`)**.\n  * It uses the local Meta model server for code generation while leaving the authoritative state and Snowball ledgers in place."}
