{"step_index":2420,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T17:01:13Z","input_tokens":2349,"cache_read_tokens":191552,"output_tokens":966,"content":"### Summary: The Modular Container Provisioning Environment Is Buttoned Up\n\nThe dedicated container repository at [`/srv/git/3tched-container`](file:///srv/git/3tched-container) is now completely self-contained, tested, and committed to `main` (`ae56f89`).\n\n---\n\n### What Has Been Created & Finalized\n\n```\n/srv/git/3tched-container/\n├── assets/\n│   └── manifest.json             # Asset coordinates, storage bucket URLs, and checksums\n├── instances/\n│   └── chatbot-template.json     # Incus JSON container template (seccomp filters, UDS lungs)\n├── profiles/\n│   └── 3tched-lungs.json         # Incus profile defining /run/opdbus/lungs socket & tmpfs\n├── storage/\n│   └── make-cozo-device.sh       # Formatter for the master 20G template (10G leaf + 10G ext4)\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── provision-identity.sh     # The complete 7-stage emergence provisioner with finish receipt\n│   ├── sync-upgrade.sh           # Boot-time atomic Btrfs OS layer upgrade helper\n│   └── launch-identity.sh        # Minimal direct launcher\n└── README.md                     # Comprehensive architecture and operation guide\n```\n\n---\n\n### The 7-Stage Emergence Lifecycle (`scripts/provision-identity.sh`)\n\nWhen you run `provision-identity.sh <instance-name> <wireguard-pubkey>`, it executes this exact, clean sequence with **zero risky live formatting**:\n\n1. **`[1/7 GENESIS]`**: Binds the cryptographic identity (Session UUID & WireGuard public key).\n2. **`[2/7 DNA]`**: Clones the pre-formatted 20 GiB sparse device via `cp --reflink=auto` (instantaneous Copy-on-Write, zero disk bloat) and randomizes the ext4 UUID (`tune2fs -U`) to prevent collisions.\n3. **`[3/7 SPINE]`**: Verifies/registers the `3tched-lungs` Incus profile.\n4. **`[4/7 GESTATION]`**: Materializes the instance specification and attaches the block device as `/dev/cozo-disk`.\n5. **`[5/7 AWAKEN]`**: Starts the container via Incus REST API.\n6. **`[6/7 BREATHE]`**: Mounts the ext4 Cozo silo (`/dev/cozo-disk2`) into `/var/lib/op-dbus` and sprouts the writable Btrfs leaf (`/dev/cozo-disk1`) onto the rootfs via `btrfs device add`.\n7. **`[7/7 RECEIPT]`**: Seals the authoritative finish receipt on disk:\n   `/var/lib/op-dbus/identity-cozo/receipts/<instance-name>.receipt.json`.\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural Invariants Enforced\n\n* **Zero Docker**: Strictly native Incus system containers.\n* **Zero Nested Btrfs on Host**: The container rootfs resides in the Incus `dir` pool over the immutable seed image, with leaf sprouting contained inside the container namespace.\n* **Ext4 Cozo Silo**: Eliminates Btrfs Copy-on-Write write amplification during RocksDB SST compactions.\n* **The Third Eye (UDS)**: No virtual NICs (`eth0`). The container communicates strictly through the Unix domain socket in its lungs.\n* **Atomic OS Upgrades**: `sync-upgrade.sh` verifies and synchronizes the OS layer via Btrfs send/receive without touching user/agent memory.\n\n---\n\n### How to Run It\n\n```bash\n# Provision a new identity container\nsudo /srv/git/3tched-container/scripts/provision-identity.sh id-1 '<wireguard_public_key>'\n\n# Inspect the generated finish receipt\ncat /var/lib/op-dbus/identity-cozo/receipts/id-1.receipt.json\n```\n\nWhenever you are ready, let me know what changes or next steps you would like to make!"}
